# Design choices:

Genereic elements:
All containers (keys/values) stroes their values in union type elem_t. 
The user is responsible for reading the same field as was written to, 
since C has no runtime type information
(ex. int_elem(2) is read back with .i)

Hash Table:
The hash table is an array of buckets (No_buckets, currenty 17) each bucket
is a singly linked list wherre every first element is a sentinel node. 
The sentinel node removes the special case needed to handle empty buckets
and makes sure we never have to read from an empty bucket (that would be undefined behavior)

Linked list:
A singly linked list with a sentinel node first and pointers to the first and last link in the list.
Makes append, prepend and size O(1). 

Iterators:
The hash table iterator visits entries in no specific order, so code using the ht_iterator
must not depend on the order. The linked list iteration however visits the elemets in order

Failiure handling:
Functions that can not signal failiure through their return values use preconditions in their 
headers and assert statments in their implementation to crach the program if a precondition is violated

