# Coverage comment:

At the moment 2026.10.09 the list_iterator_remove function has not yet been implemeted (it was optional). This lowers the coverage percentage of the list_iterator.c file. 

In the iterator.c file, the ioopm_hash_table_iterator_advance function has a precondition that states that we must be positioned at a valid entry. To ensure this precondition is not violated there is an if statement that states if the current entry is equal to NULL, we dont advance the iterator further. This path is never tested in the iterator_tests.c file. Therefore the lower coverage. 

The branches not taken are in all files either assert statements or if statement. In both cases the statements are there to make sure no precondition is violated. 

